---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="ALL-LLLM Pod — Transcript Intelligence">
  <main class="ti-page">
    <a class="back" href="/projects/all-lllm-pod/">← ALL-LLLM Pod</a>

    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">TRANSCRIPT INTELLIGENCE</p>
      <h1>Transcript Forensics and Repair</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        The first run of <strong>ALL-LLLM POD</strong> transcripts used a WhisperX / NeMo
        hybrid pipeline built around a deliberate architectural choice.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <div class="architecture">
        <div>
          <strong>WhisperX timestamps are canonical.</strong>
          <p>
            ASR is the sole authority on <em>what</em> was said and <em>when</em> it was said.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>NeMo answers who spoke.</strong>
          <p>
            Speaker identity is assigned by majority vote only within the boundaries
            WhisperX created. Hard-applying NeMo RTTM boundaries produced highly
            fragmented transcripts that required unreasonable effort to repair.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        The first generation of human-in-the-loop tooling was built in late 2025.
        Diarization-generated <code>SPEAKER_IDs</code> were first mapped to host identities
        using
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UPnnOCWqiAw" target="_blank">Clownfish ↗</a>.
        The transcript was then inspected for structural artifacts such as ellipses,
        non-terminating sentences, and lowercase continuations — signals that speaker
        attribution may have broken down.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2025 HITL (Production)</h2>

      <article class="case">
        <p class="case-label">01 · TURN CONTAMINATION</p>
        <h3>Ellipsis boundary</h3>

        <p>
          A segment presents as one speaker having a continuous thought — but in reality,
          two speakers exist within it. Fingerprint: mid-segment ellipsis. The most common
          structural cue, but rare false-positives exist.
          <a href="https://www.loom.com/share/65827f1c9f3f419cac6dd8b544657ca2" target="_blank">↗ example</a>
        </p>

        <p class="source">
          X-Sb8sIi22g · 699.069s ·
          <a href="https://youtu.be/X-Sb8sIi22g?t=693" target="_blank">episode ↗</a>
        </p>

        <div class="diff">
          <div class="panel before">
            <span class="panel-label">BEFORE</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            Interest rates just have to go up to a point that
            <span class="flagged">… To</span> what's happening in Japan, right?
          </div>

          <div class="panel after">
            <span class="panel-label">AFTER</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            Interest rates just have to go up to a point that
            <span class="flagged">…</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            <span class="flagged">To</span> what's happening in Japan, right?
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <p class="case-label">02 · TURN CONTAMINATION</p>
        <h3>Speaker sandwich</h3>

        <p>
          Three segments, two speakers, A→B→A. The middle segment (B) is a misattribution —
          B never spoke. Fingerprint: middle segment ends with ellipsis, third segment opens lowercase.
        </p>

        <p class="source">
          AI_Psychosis__America_s_Broken_Soci_WOWLT.json · 94.608s–103.266s ·
          <a href="https://youtu.be/Oy4evu1TdiI?t=92" target="_blank">episode ↗</a>
        </p>

        <div class="diff">
          <div class="panel before">
            <span class="panel-label">BEFORE</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            I think they did a great job.
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            It's like one of those <span class="flagged">weird...</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            <span class="flagged">you know,</span> superhero groups that it's like a real throwback.
          </div>

          <div class="panel after">
            <span class="panel-label">AFTER</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            I think they did a great job.
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            It's like one of those <span class="flagged">weird...</span>
            <span class="flagged">you know,</span> superhero groups that it's like a real throwback.
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <p class="case-label">03 · SPEAKER IDENTITY</p>
        <h3>Third-person self-reference</h3>

        <p>
          The attributed speaker's own name appears in their own segment — a strong signal
          the segment belongs to someone else. Unlike boundary heuristics, no ellipsis or
          capitalization signal is required. The name alone is the fingerprint.
        </p>

        <p class="source">
          episode data · 4035.425s ·
          <a href="https://youtu.be/X-Sb8sIi22g?t=4034" target="_blank">episode ↗</a>
        </p>

        <div class="diff">
          <div class="panel before">
            <span class="panel-label">BEFORE</span>
            <span class="spk">Friedberg</span>
            Less than the $1.4 billion in funding it has raised to
            <span class="flagged">Friedberg's</span> been bringing this point up over and over about the
            overfunding and cash in less than the valuation most yeah of these unicorns are worth less
            than their total press stack and this is a good example I've been through this week I went
            and saw a company I was an investor in that I saw this happen
          </div>

          <div class="panel after">
            <span class="panel-label">AFTER</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            Less than the $1.4 billion in funding it has raised to
            <span class="flagged">Friedberg's</span> been bringing this point up over and over about the
            overfunding and cash in less than the valuation most
            <span class="spk">Friedberg</span>
            yeah of these unicorns are worth less than their total press stack and this is a good example
            I've been through this week I went and saw a company I was an investor in that I saw this happen
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <p class="case-label">04 · CONTINUATION ERROR</p>
        <h3>Lowercase continuation</h3>

        <p>
          ASR capitalizes new speaker turns — a lowercase opening strongly suggests this is
          a continuation misattributed to a different speaker.
        </p>

        <p class="source">
          500K_Subscriber_Livestream____AllIn_WOWLT.json · 411.02s–436.16s ·
          <a href="https://youtu.be/AsDrfUQImhs?t=410" target="_blank">episode ↗</a>
        </p>

        <div class="diff">
          <div class="panel before">
            <span class="panel-label">BEFORE</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            So when he meets with business people, they're all like, oh, I just saw you on the
            <span class="flagged">All-In Pod.</span>
            <span class="spk">Chamath</span>
            <span class="flagged">so uh he was saying</span> he said we have a big hit on our hands he said uh
            he said we're like tv stars now that's incredible imagine if uh if we had if we didn't have to push
            sand uphill with some of these folks...
          </div>

          <div class="panel after">
            <span class="panel-label">AFTER</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            So when he meets with business people, they're all like, oh, I just saw you on the
            <span class="flagged">All-In Pod. so uh he was saying</span> he said we have a big hit on our hands
            he said uh he said we're like tv stars now.
            <span class="spk">Chamath</span>
            now that's incredible imagine if uh if we had if we didn't have to push sand uphill with some
            of these folks...
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="case">
        <p class="case-label">05 · BACKCHANNEL BLEED</p>
        <h3>Short utterances lose their speaker</h3>

        <p>
          Short affirmative utterances in rapid exchange fall below the reliable embedding
          window and get misassigned to the acoustically dominant local speaker. The boundaries
          are correct, the words are right — the embeddings simply don't have enough audio to
          build a clean voiceprint.
        </p>

        <p class="source">
          500K_Subscriber_Livestream____AllIn_WOWLT.json · 354.645s–369.541s ·
          <a href="https://youtu.be/AsDrfUQImhs?t=354" target="_blank">episode ↗</a>
        </p>

        <div class="diff">
          <div class="panel before">
            <span class="panel-label">BEFORE</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            Well, I said that even my co-hosts who aren't fans of his had to admit he did a good job.
            And he said, well, tell them I said hi too.
            <span class="flagged">Oh, okay.</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            So you sandbagged us with the president.
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            <span class="flagged">Got it.</span>
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            Thank you.
          </div>

          <div class="panel after">
            <span class="panel-label">AFTER</span>
            <span class="spk">Sacks</span>
            Well, I said that even my co-hosts who aren't fans of his had to admit he did a good job.
            And he said, well, tell them I said hi too.
            <span class="spk">Jcal</span>
            <span class="flagged">Oh, okay.</span> So you sandbagged us with the president.
            <span class="flagged">Got it.</span> Thank you.
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2026 — Word-level acoustics</h2>

      <p>
        The next layer applies NeMo diarization at the word level inside existing WhisperX
        segments. Instead of asking only whether a segment looks structurally suspicious,
        the system can ask whether individual words acoustically resemble the speaker they
        were assigned to.
      </p>

      <p>
        The benefit is higher transcript fidelity and resolution down to word-level
        atomics. The tradeoff is more review work and greater operational complexity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <a class="project-back" href="/projects/all-lllm-pod/">←</a>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ti-page {
    width: min(100% - 32px, 980px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 0 96px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .hero {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-bottom: 54px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .case-label,
  .panel-label,
  .source {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .case-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 8px 0 18px;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  section {
    margin: 0 0 64px;
  }

  section > p {
    max-width: 800px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .architecture {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }

  .architecture > div {
    border-left: 4px solid #111;
    padding: 4px 0 4px 18px;
  }

  .architecture p {
    margin: 7px 0 0;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .case {
    margin: 34px 0 52px;
  }

  .case h3 {
    margin: 6px 0 12px;
  }

  .case > p {
    max-width: 800px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .source {
    margin: 14px 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .diff {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }



  .project-back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .architecture,
    .diff {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .ti-page {
      width: min(100% - 24px, 980px);
    }
  }

  .panel {
    background: #0d1117;
    border: 1px solid #1e2530;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #c9d1d9;
  }

  .before {
    border-top: 2px solid #c0392b;
  }

  .after {
    border-top: 2px solid #0A84FF;
  }

  .panel-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .before .panel-label {
    color: #e74c3c;
  }

  .after .panel-label {
    color: #0A84FF;
  }

  .spk {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #8b9eb0;
  }

  .spk:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .before .flagged {
    color: #ff6b6b;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .after .flagged {
    color: #a8d672;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

</style>
